  23:       backgrounds.
  24:     - The enclosed background components form a complete rectangular array of
  25:       slots, ordered by their positions.
  26:     - Each slot contains either no other color or exactly one object color.
  27: 
  28:     Rule
  29:     - Find all 4-connected components of the most common color that do not touch
  30:       the input edge.
  31:     - Sort their bounding boxes into row and column order to define the output
  32:       table.
  33:     - For each slot, output its unique non-background color if present; otherwise
  34:       output the background color.
  35: 
  36:     Key insight
  37:     - The large grid is an expanded table: the enclosed background components are
  38:       the cells, and any colored object drawn inside a cell is that cell's summary
  39:       value.
  40:     """
  41:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  42:     assert g.ndim == 2, "expected a 2D grid"
  43:     height, width = map(int, g.shape)
  44: 
  45:     bg = get_bg(g)
